Two-Headed Giant (Commander Duels v0.5.1 card audit), part 3: the rules the audit found missing.

Reason: v0.5.0's patches 0001 and 0002 made teams take turns and share life, but XMage still reads one
active player in many rules, so cards that name "each player's" step, "your turn", a skip, turn
control, "can't lose", poison counts or the attacking player played wrong for the teammate of the
turn's holder. With this, in a game that names teammates (Game.getTeammates, from part 1):
- 805.4d, 805.9: the beginning of a step or phase is checked for each player of the active team
  (TeamStepEvent). An ability worded for "each player's" or "each opponent's" step that refers to
  "that player" triggers once for each of them (TriggeredAbility.triggersForEachTeamPlayer, by the
  rules text for AtStepTriggeredAbility); any other triggers once, at the first of the team's players
  it applies to, so "your upkeep" triggers for the holder's teammate too, and an enchanted player's
  step is that player's. While such an ability triggers, goes on the stack and resolves, the player
  whose step it is is "the active player" for it (805.9: Game.asActivePlayer), so an effect that
  reads the active player acts for that player.
- 805.9: "not your turn" (NotMyTurnCondition) and the core's other "your turn" checks read the team's
  turn; each player of the active team may play the extra lands an effect gives "each player".
- 805.8: a turn, phase or step a player of the active team skips, or an extra phase or step they get,
  is the team's (TurnMods.useNextForTeam; Step.skipStep and Phase.skipPhase ask for each team player;
  a turn a teammate skips, Time Vault); controlling a player controls their whole team.
- 805.10a, 805.10c: each player of the active team is an attacking player (Combat.isAttackingPlayer,
  getAttackers(player), getAttackingPlayerOf); "you attack" counts the creatures you control.
- 810.8a: a team can't lose (or win) when an effect says one of its players can't; no one on a team
  loses for having 0 or less life when an effect says one of them doesn't.
- 810.9d, 810.9e: an effect that sets each player's life total sets one per team, chosen by the team
  (Game.chooseLifeTotalsToSet); teammates can't exchange life totals.
- 810.10a, 810.10b: poison counts and the 704.5c loss read the team's counters (Game.getPoisonCounters,
  getPoisonCountersToLose, public, replacing part 2's protected methods); poison counters a player
  loses beyond their own come off their teammates'.
- Assist: a teammate's mana counts as help, and a computer teammate helps pay.
Every other game type names no teammates, and each change reduces to XMage's own code there.
Needs parts 1 and 2.
Upstream: none yet; to be offered to magefree/mage with parts 1 to 3.
Remove when: XMage upstream implements Two-Headed Giant, or the format is dropped.

